<title>HONG KONG: HKSE says welcomes China's new rule on listings.</title>
<headline>HKSE says welcomes China's new rule on listings.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Hong Kong Stock Exchange said on Monday it welcomed the announcement by China's State Council on the listings by mainland enterprises in overseas markets.</p>
<p>The stock exchange said in a statement it believed the move would further clarify matters relating to the regulation of the share issues and listings by Chinese firms.</p>
<p>It said the stock exchange and the Securities and Future Commission had been participating in discussions with Chinese regulators, the China Securities Regulatory Commission, on the matters.</p>
<p>On Friday, China had issued to provincial and municipal governments a further notice on strengthening the regulation of share issues and listings in overseas markets.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6441  http://www.hk97.com</p>
